==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|machinatus|lang=la}}, past participle of {{term|machinari||to contrive, plan, devise, plot, scheme}}, from {{term|machina||a machine, contrivance, device, scheme}}; see [[machine]].

===Verb===
{{en-verb|machinat|ing}}

# (''transitive'' or ''intransitive'') To [[devise]] a [[plot]] or [[secret]] [[plan]]; to [[conspire]].
#* '''2011'', Ian Douglas Robertson, ''Turtle Hawks''
#*: Had she already managed to '''machinate''' a cushy job for her husband?

